downstream coordination, the readiness matrix, and build pipeline work build on.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- For each of `ubi9/python-311`, `ubi9/python-312`, `ubi9/nodejs-22`, and the RHEL 9.8 rebase: a committed availability date is recorded, or a determination is recorded that the dependency will not be available before September 15, 2026.\n- Any published candidate PQC base image recommended for adoption is verified to report `DEFAULT:PQ` when queried with `update-crypto-policies --show` inside the image.\n- If no committed date exists for any dependency by early September, an escalation is raised to leadership so affected teams can pivot to OCP exception filing before the deadline.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1 [P0]** (all RHOAI runtime images use a PQC-enabled base image): this investigation determines the compliance path (switch vs. exception) for the python/nodejs-based and RHEL9-ELS-based image groups.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":60809,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b14d6098c05a58eb","agent_id":"a8bd95be9a2e5f76c","session_id":"12e54bbc-7543-4961-a6e8-72b51d0a133c","uuid":"93cccbe2-7238-42fe-9406-60d1c442e72c","timestamp":"2026-10-22T11:48:12.903Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8001"}
