{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-36cbc711-407e-4d11-9634-10ba4b53ac0c","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-93ea4fd1f202e845","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8001-2pydiqur/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8001-BRANCH-A-E006.md","content":"# Integrate confirmed PQC variant base images into the build pipeline and coordinate team switches\n\n*Conditional branch A — applies if PQC variants of the python-311/312/nodejs bases and/or the RHEL 9.8 rebase are confirmed available before September 15, 2026.*\n\n## Description\n\nWhen the PQC base image availability investigation confirms that PQC variants of `ubi9/python-311`, `ubi9/python-312`, `ubi9/nodejs-22` and/or the RHEL 9.8 rebase (enabling `rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal` adoption) will be available in time, this epic wires those newly confirmed base images into the RHOAI build pipeline — extending the pipeline enablement already in place for the confirmed bases — and coordinates the affected component teams' final-runtime-stage switches. Affected images: ~10 python-based training variants/lmes-job/feature-server images, 1 nodejs-based dashboard image, and ~34 RHEL9-ELS-based notebooks/workbenches/training-runtime/mlserver images.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Integrate each newly confirmed PQC base image variant into the RHOAI build pipeline, building on the base image pipeline updates already established for the confirmed PQC bases.\n- Notify the owning component teams of each confirmed variant (python-311: 5 training/lmes-job images; python-312: 4 training variants; python-312-minimal: feature-server; nodejs-22: dashboard; RHEL9-ELS group post-rebase) to switch their final runtime stage.\n- Update the readiness matrix records for the switched image groups.\n- For any group in a partial outcome (some variants confirmed, others not), coordinate the switch only for confirmed groups — unconfirmed groups follow the OCP exception path instead.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Each confirmed PQC base image variant is referenceable by RHOAI component builds in the build pipeline.\n- Affected component teams are notified with the specific target base image for their images and the final-stage-only constraint (only the runtime stage changes; no builder image change — HLR-3).\n- Readiness matrix records for the switched groups are updated to reflect the confirmed path.\n- Switched images report `DEFAULT:PQ` via `update-crypto-policies --show` and list ML-KEM-512/768/1024 via `openssl list -kem-algorithms` (OpenSSL-backed components).\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1 [P0]**: delivers the switch path for the python/nodejs-based and RHEL9-ELS-based image groups when their PQC bases are confirmed.\n- **HLR-3 [P0]**: switches are final-runtime-stage-only.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":64685,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b14d6098c05a58eb","agent_id":"a8bd95be9a2e5f76c","session_id":"12e54bbc-7543-4961-a6e8-72b51d0a133c","uuid":"ed3b45fb-5cb1-485a-af8e-7f9ca43899ac","timestamp":"2026-10-22T11:49:18.079Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8001"}
