ngs to acknowledgment, and update the readiness matrix records for images on the exception path.\n- In partial outcomes, only unconfirmed groups follow this path — confirmed groups switch base images instead.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Every affected component team has filed an OCP exception via OCPEXCEPT by September 15, 2026, including the component's TLS stack, the reason it cannot negotiate ML-KEM, and a documented remediation plan.\n- Exception filings are tracked to acknowledgment.\n- Readiness matrix records for exception-path images are updated to reflect the filed exceptions.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-2 [P0]**: delivers the exception path for teams unable to comply by September 15.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":65458,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b14d6098c05a58eb","agent_id":"a8bd95be9a2e5f76c","session_id":"12e54bbc-7543-4961-a6e8-72b51d0a133c","uuid":"10a17dfb-a116-44bd-846e-10abb4be4444","timestamp":"2026-10-22T11:49:30.033Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8001"}
