{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b0377868174e56dd","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8001\n3\tepic_count: 5\n4\tcritical_path_length: 3\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\trevised: false\n7\ttriage: null\n8\ttriage_rationale: null\n9\t---\n10\t# RHAISTRAT-8001 Decomposition — Base Image Compliance: Post-Quantum Cryptography Support\n11\t\n12\t## Strategy Summary\n13\t\n14\tRHAISTRAT-8001 is a **compliance coordination tracker** for switching all RHOAI runtime images to PQC-enabled base images by **September 15, 2026** (RHOAI 3.6 / OCP 5.0), or filing an OCP exception via OCPEXCEPT. Two PQC base images are confirmed available (`ubi9/ubi-minimal-pqc`, `rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal`); PQC variants of the python-311/312 and nodejs-22 bases are unconfirmed (RHOAIENG-7195 / AIPCC), and the AIPCC RHEL 9.8 rebase (AIPCC-7258) gates RHEL9-ELS image adoption.\n15\t\n16\t## Scope Notes (read before reviewing epic coverage)\n17\t\n18\t- **Per-team switch and exception-filing work is deliberately NOT decomposed into per-team epics.** The strategy explicitly delegates it: \"Implementation work is owned by each component team\", \"OCP exception filing for individual teams — each team files their own\", and the mechanism is \"teams link their tracking tickets to RHAISTRAT-8001\". HLR-1/HLR-2 coverage is therefore achieved through the coordination, readiness-matrix, pipeline-enablement, and deadline-enforcement epics below — not through ~150 per-team epics the strategy provides no team→image mapping for.\n19\t- **Not triaged below-threshold** (Step 0): although the effort estimate is S, the strategy affects all RHOAI component images across multiple teams (fails single-component/single-team), and it contains genuine unknowns (unconfirmed PQC base variants, RHEL 9.8 rebase timing) whose answers change which downstream work exists.\n20\t- **Not docs-only** (Step 0): affected components require code/config/pipeline changes (owned by teams), plus coordination deliverables owned here.\n21\t- Go ML-KEM, TLSAdherence, and TLS-scanner CI are owned by RHAISTRAT-7816 (out of scope). ML-DSA certificates are deferred (HLR-4, not mapped).\n22\t\n23\t## Epic List (main plan)\n24\t\n25\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n26\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n27\t| RHAISTRAT-8001-E001 | Confirm PQC base image variant availability and RHEL 9.8 rebase timing with AIPCC | Investigation | AIPCC team | P0 |\n28\t| RHAISTRAT-8001-E002 | Enable confirmed PQC base images in the RHOAI build pipeline | Implementation | DevOps/Build | P0 |\n29\t| RHAISTRAT-8001-E003 | Author the PQC Readiness Matrix per component | Implementation | RHOAI PM | P0 |\n30\t| RHAISTRAT-8001-E004 | Track component team compliance and enforce the September 15 deadline | Implementation | RHOAI PM | P0 |\n31\t| RHAISTRAT-8001-E005 | Define the PQC TLS handshake performance regression threshold and validate latency | Investigation | Performance team | P1 |\n32\t\n33\t### Conditional branch epics (gated by E001 outcome; not standalone Jira issues)\n34\t\n35\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority | Branch |\n36\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|--------|\n37\t| RHAISTRAT-8001-BRANCH-A-E006 | Integrate confirmed PQC variant base images into the build pipeline and coordinate team switches | Implementation | DevOps/Build | P0 | A — variants/rebase confirmed in time |\n38\t| RHAISTRAT-8001-BRANCH-B-E006 | Coordinate OCP exception filings for images without available PQC base images | Implementation | RHOAI PM | P0 | B — variants/rebase not available in time |\n39\t\n40\t## Dependency DAG\n41\t\n42\t```mermaid\n43\tgraph TD\n44\t    E001[\"E001 Investigation: PQC variant + rebase availability\"]\n45\t    E002[\"E002 Pipeline: confirmed PQC bases\"]\n46\t    E003[\"E003 PQC Readiness Matrix\"]\n47\t    E004[\"E004 Compliance tracking + deadline enforcement\"]\n48\t    E005[\"E005 Investigation: perf threshold + validation\"]\n49\t    BA[\"BRANCH-A-E006 Variant switch path (branch A)\"]\n50\t    BB[\"BRANCH-B-E006 Exception path (branch B)\"]\n51\t\n52\t    E001 --> E003\n53\t    E003 --> E004\n54\t    E001 --> BA\n55\t    E002 --> BA\n56\t    E001 --> BB\n57\t```\n58\t\n59\tMain-plan critical path: **E001 → E003 → E004** (length 3). Branch epics are excluded from the main-plan critical path.\n60\t\n61\t## DAG Justification\n62\t\n63\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n64\t|------|------|-----------|\n65\t| E001 → E003 | Rule 3 (Investigation gates downstream) | The readiness matrix's per-image remediation path (switch vs. exception) for ~45 python/nodejs-based and RHEL9-ELS-based images is determined by the investigation outcome. True gate: `rewrite` — matrix content changes, epic exists either way. |\n66\t| E003 → E004 | Rule 12/13 (artifact consumer) | Deadline enforcement and the \"zero unaccounted images\" close-out audit consume the readiness matrix as the per-image accounting artifact. |\n67\t| E001 → BRANCH-A-E006 | Rule 3 (conditional branch) | Branch A only exists if PQC variants and the rebase are confirmed in time (bounded outcome, ≤3 possibilities → conditional branch). |\n68\t| E002 → BRANCH-A-E006 | Rule 13 / epic boundary (same surface) | Branch A builds on the build-pipeline base-image wiring for the same build configuration surface; serial to avoid two epics editing the same pipeline configuration independently. |\n69\t| E001 → BRANCH-B-E006 | Rule 3 (conditional branch) | Branch B only exists if variants/rebase are not available in time; affected teams are directed to the OCP exception path. |\n70\t| No edge E001 → E002 | Rule 17 / Step 5.5 (tiered delivery) | The two confirmed base images (`ubi9-minimal-pqc`, `rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal`) enable Tier 1 partial value now; pipeline enablement for them does not wait on the investigation. |\n71\t| No edge E005 → any epic | Rule 4 / Step 6.5 | The performance threshold does not change which epics exist or what they do — the switch and coordination work proceeds the same way; the threshold defines ship-gating pass/fail. Kept as an Investigation because the strategy explicitly flags it \"NEEDS DOMAIN INPUT\" with owners (PM + Performance team lead) and a resolution deadline (before Sprint 2 ends); runs in parallel. |\n72\t| No konflux/repo-onboarding edges | Rules 5–10 | No new component or repository is provisioned by this strategy; all work happens in existing repos, Jira, and existing build infrastructure. N/A. |\n73\t\n74\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n75\t\n76\t| HLR | Priority | Epics |\n77\t|-----|----------|-------|\n78\t| HLR-1: All RHOAI runtime images use a PQC-enabled base image | P0 | E002 (pipeline enablement for confirmed bases), E003 (matrix records per-image target base), BRANCH-A-E006 (switch path for variant-gated images), E004 (compliance verification and close-out). Per-team switch execution is delegated to component teams via linked tracking tickets (see Scope Notes). |\n79\t| HLR-2: Teams unable to comply file an OCP exception by September 15 with remediation plan | P0 | BRANCH-B-E006 (exception-filing coordination), E004 (zero-unaccounted-images enforcement). Per-team filing is delegated (see Scope Notes). |\n80\t| HLR-3: PQC enablement is runtime only — only the final stage changes, no builder image change | P0 | E002 (consumption guidance reflects final-stage-only switch), E003 (matrix documents the final-stage-only change per component), BRANCH-A-E006 (acceptance criterion). |\n81\t| HLR-4: PQC-signed X.509 certificates (ML-DSA) | Deferred | Not mapped — explicitly deferred to a follow-on phase (strategy out-of-scope). |\n82\t\n83\t## Conditional Branches\n84\t\n85\tE001 has two bounded outcomes that change downstream structure:\n86\t\n87\t- **Branch A — PQC variants and/or RHEL 9.8 rebase confirmed available before September 15, 2026**: `RHAISTRAT-8001-BRANCH-A-E006` — wire the confirmed variant base images into the build pipeline and coordinate affected teams' final-stage switches.\n88\t- **Branch B — variants/rebase not available in time**: `RHAISTRAT-8001-BRANCH-B-E006` — coordinate OCP exception filings (with TLS stack and remediation plan) for affected images.\n89\t\n90\tBoth branch epics set `branch`, `gated_by=RHAISTRAT-8001-E001` (also in `dependencies`), and `gate_failure_impact` (`remove` — each branch epic does not exist if the other outcome holds). Partial outcomes (e.g., rebase lands but nodejs variant slips) are handled per image group: confirmed groups follow Branch A, unconfirmed groups follow Branch B; the fallback_approach text on each branch epic states this. `epic_count` counts the 5 main-plan epics; the 2 branch epics are additional.\n91\t\n92\t## Health Warnings\n93\t\n94\t1. **Scope trap — AC-1 measurement infrastructure**: AC-1 is \"measured by automated CI scan across the RHOAI 3.6 payload\", but TLS-scanner CI is owned by RHAISTRAT-7816 (out of scope). The verification is carried as an acceptance criterion on E004 with a cross-strategy dependency note; if RHAISTRAT-7816 does not deliver scan tooling, the measurement mechanism for AC-1 is unowned.\n95\t2. **Priority inversion risk — performance NFR**: The performance NFR is marked \"NEEDS DOMAIN INPUT\", is ship-gating (\"must be resolved before Sprint 2 ends\", Performance Team Support: Required), yet no HLR carries it. It is modeled as a P1 Investigation (E005) running parallel to the P0 coordination chain; if leadership treats it as ship-blocking, its effective priority exceeds its label.\n96\t3. **NFR vs. scope contradiction — Rust TLS migration**: The Security NFR requires fms-guardrails-orchestrator (and any pure-Rust TLS components) to \"support ML-KEM hybrid key exchange after migration\", but no Rust TLS migration is scheduled in this strategy's scope; architecture context confirms rustls+ring with no OpenSSL in the release image. Remediation ownership is delegated to component teams via OCP exception remediation plans (TLS migration spike RHOAIENG-7452). The NFR cannot be satisfied by this strategy's epics alone.\n97\t4. **Unresolved trainer data cache TLS posture**: \"Rust TLS posture unknown\" (audit spike RHOAIENG-7196). Tracked as an input/acceptance criterion on the readiness matrix (E003) rather than a new Investigation epic, because an existing spike (RHOAIENG-7196) already owns the question.\n98\t5. **Strategy-level process gates pending**: Architecture Review, ODH/RHOAI Build Onboarding, Licence Validation, and Documentation Support are all \"Pending human review\" — these human gates are unresolved at the strategy level and may re-scope downstream work.\n99\t6. **Missing standard sections**: The strategy has no formal Affected Components table (component, change, owner) — components are described in prose (\"All RHOAI component images\") with the image inventory delegated to external links. Proceeded with available information.\n100\t\n101\t## Tiered Delivery\n102\t\n103\tExternal dependency (PQC python/nodejs base variants, AIPCC RHEL 9.8 rebase) has uncertain timing, and partial value is deliverable without it:\n104\t\n105\t- **Tier 1 (independent, start immediately)**:\n106\t  - E001 — risk-reduction Investigation with AIPCC (escalation trigger: no committed date by early September).\n107\t  - E002 — build pipeline can consume the two confirmed PQC base images; the ~68 `ubi9-minimal`-based images can be switched by their teams now.\n108\t  - E005 — performance threshold definition and validation (independent of base variant availability).\n109\t- **Tier 2 (dependency-gated by E001)**:\n110\t  - E003, E004 — readiness matrix consolidation and deadline close-out (need resolved switch-vs-exception paths).\n111\t  - BRANCH-A-E006 / BRANCH-B-E006 — the conditional compliance path for python/nodejs-based (~11 images) and RHEL9-ELS-based (~34 images, gated on the rebase) images.\n112\t\n113\t## Component Mapping Notes (non-obvious)\n114\t\n115\tStrategy components are platform-wide (\"All RHOAI component images\"); canonical `.context/rhai-components.txt` names assigned per epic:\n116\t\n117\t| Strategy term | Canonical component |\n118\t|---------------|--------------------|\n119\t| AIPCC team (PQC base variant confirmation/delivery) | AIPCC Productization |\n120\t| DevOps/Build team (base image pipeline updates) | Build and Release |\n121\t| Platform-wide PQC compliance coordination, readiness matrix, deadline enforcement | AI Core Platform Security |\n122\t| Performance team (TLS handshake regression threshold/measurement) | PerfScale |\n123\t\n124\tSupporting architecture context used: `fms-guardrails-orchestrator.md` (rustls+ring, non-FIPS-validated, no OpenSSL in release image), `PLATFORM.md` (FIPS posture, component runtime summary), `trainer.md` (Go operator, cluster TLS security profile usage).\n125\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac1ecaaf3df4b37e","agent_id":"a3b5f159801f9c1af","session_id":"12e54bbc-7543-4961-a6e8-72b51d0a133c","uuid":"aa6f14bf-2275-45ca-b120-787798704444","timestamp":"2026-10-22T11:53:04.960Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b0377868174e56dd","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8001 decomposition"}
