{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bcab81ca6b958988","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8001-E001\n3\ttitle: Confirm PQC base image variant availability and RHEL 9.8 rebase timing with\n4\t  AIPCC\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8001\n6\tcomponent: AIPCC Productization\n7\tteam: AIPCC team\n8\ttype: Investigation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 0\n13\t  local_runnability: 1\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n15\t  human_judgment_required: -2\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tdependencies: []\n18\tai_signals: null\n19\tai_implementability: Medium\n20\tai_implementability_score: 0\n21\tjira_key: null\n22\tbranch: null\n23\tgated_by: null\n24\tgate_failure_impact: null\n25\t---\n26\t# Confirm PQC base image variant availability and RHEL 9.8 rebase timing with AIPCC\n27\t\n28\t## Description\n29\t\n30\tThis investigation resolves the strategy's gating unknowns around unconfirmed PQC base images: whether PQC variants of `ubi9/python-311`, `ubi9/python-312`, and `ubi9/nodejs-22` will be published before the September 15, 2026 compliance deadline, and the committed date for the AIPCC RHEL 9.8 rebase (AIPCC-7258) that gates adoption of `rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal` for ~34 RHEL9-ELS-based images. It is tracked alongside the AIPCC spike RHOAIENG-7195. The outcome determines, per image group, whether component teams switch their final runtime stage to a PQC base or must file an OCP exception — i.e., it selects between the switch path and the exception path for roughly 45 RHOAI images.\n31\t\n32\t## Scope\n33\t\n34\t- Confirm with the AIPCC team whether PQC variants of `ubi9/python-311`, `ubi9/python-312`, and `ubi9/nodejs-22` (5 + 4 + 1 RHOAI images respectively) will be available before September 15, 2026, and obtain committed delivery dates.\n35\t- Confirm the committed date of the AIPCC RHEL 9.8 rebase (AIPCC-7258), which gates RHEL9-ELS PQC base image adoption for notebooks, workbenches, training runtimes, and mlserver (~34 images).\n36\t- Verify, where candidate images are already published, that they report `DEFAULT:PQ` crypto policy (e.g., by inspecting the published image directly).\n37\t- Escalate if no committed date is obtained by early September (per the strategy's risk mitigation).\n38\t- Deliverable: a recorded determination per image group — \"PQC base available by deadline (with date)\" or \"not available by deadline\" — that downstream coordination, the readiness matrix, and build pipeline work build on.\n39\t\n40\t## Acceptance Criteria\n41\t\n42\t- For each of `ubi9/python-311`, `ubi9/python-312`, `ubi9/nodejs-22`, and the RHEL 9.8 rebase: a committed availability date is recorded, or a determination is recorded that the dependency will not be available before September 15, 2026.\n43\t- Any published candidate PQC base image recommended for adoption is verified to report `DEFAULT:PQ` when queried with `update-crypto-policies --show` inside the image.\n44\t- If no committed date exists for any dependency by early September, an escalation is raised to leadership so affected teams can pivot to OCP exception filing before the deadline.\n45\t\n46\t## HLR Traceability\n47\t\n48\t- **HLR-1 [P0]** (all RHOAI runtime images use a PQC-enabled base image): this investigation determines the compliance path (switch vs. exception) for the python/nodejs-based and RHEL9-ELS-based image groups.\n49\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac1ecaaf3df4b37e","agent_id":"a3b5f159801f9c1af","session_id":"12e54bbc-7543-4961-a6e8-72b51d0a133c","uuid":"cd94a773-40f6-4175-8a8d-b11182516c03","timestamp":"2026-10-22T11:53:09.414Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-bcab81ca6b958988","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8001 decomposition"}
