{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-93bb3ef9b72746ab","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8001-E002\n3\ttitle: Enable confirmed PQC base images in the RHOAI build pipeline\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8001\n5\tcomponent: Build and Release\n6\tteam: DevOps/Build\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 0\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 1\n15\t  external_dependency: 1\n16\t  human_process_gates: 0\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Enable confirmed PQC base images in the RHOAI build pipeline\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tMake the two confirmed PQC-enabled base images — `registry.redhat.io/ubi9/ubi-minimal-pqc` and `registry.redhat.io/rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal` — consumable by RHOAI component builds, so that component teams can switch the final runtime stage of their images (~68 `ubi9-minimal`-based images and, once the RHEL 9.8 rebase lands, ~34 RHEL9-ELS-based images) without each team solving build-infrastructure problems independently. This is Tier 1 work: it does not wait on the unconfirmed python/nodejs PQC variants.\n34\t\n35\t## Scope\n36\t\n37\t- Coordinate base image pipeline updates with the DevOps/Build team so the confirmed PQC base images are referenced/mirrored and available in the RHOAI build infrastructure (RHOAI-Build-Config and associated build pipelines).\n38\t- Ensure the pipeline change reflects that PQC enablement is runtime only: only the final stage of each Dockerfile/Containerfile changes; no builder image change is needed.\n39\t- Provide component teams clear consumption guidance for the confirmed PQC base images (which base to switch to, per the strategy's base image mapping).\n40\t- Note: adoption of `rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal` by component teams remains gated by the AIPCC RHEL 9.8 rebase; pipeline readiness for it can proceed in parallel.\n41\t\n42\t## Acceptance Criteria\n43\t\n44\t- The confirmed PQC base images (`ubi9/ubi-minimal-pqc`, `rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal`) are available to and referenceable by RHOAI component builds in the build pipeline.\n45\t- A component team switching only its final runtime stage to `ubi9/ubi-minimal-pqc` can build its image through the standard RHOAI build pipeline without build-infrastructure changes on their side.\n46\t- Consumption guidance published to component teams states explicitly that only the final runtime stage changes and no builder image change is required (HLR-3).\n47\t- Build pipeline behavior (including HA characteristics) is unchanged apart from the base image availability (NFR: Availability).\n48\t\n49\t## HLR Traceability\n50\t\n51\t- **HLR-1 [P0]**: enables the base image switch for all images whose target PQC base is already confirmed.\n52\t- **HLR-3 [P0]**: pipeline and guidance encode the runtime-only, final-stage-only constraint.\n53\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac1ecaaf3df4b37e","agent_id":"a3b5f159801f9c1af","session_id":"12e54bbc-7543-4961-a6e8-72b51d0a133c","uuid":"670aa71f-82a3-48c4-b9e5-3976bdbeee57","timestamp":"2026-10-22T11:53:10.389Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-93bb3ef9b72746ab","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8001 decomposition"}
