{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b2196225c1eb4daa","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8001-E005\n3\ttitle: Define the PQC TLS handshake performance regression threshold and validate\n4\t  latency\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8001\n6\tcomponent: PerfScale\n7\tteam: Performance team\n8\ttype: Investigation\n9\tpriority: P1\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 0\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 1\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: 0\n15\t  human_judgment_required: -2\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tdependencies: []\n18\tai_signals: null\n19\tai_implementability: Medium\n20\tai_implementability_score: 0\n21\tjira_key: null\n22\tbranch: null\n23\tgated_by: null\n24\tgate_failure_impact: null\n25\t---\n26\t# Define the PQC TLS handshake performance regression threshold and validate latency\n27\t\n28\t## Description\n29\t\n30\tResolve the strategy's flagged performance unknown (\"NEEDS DOMAIN INPUT — no numeric regression threshold set\"): work with the PM and Performance team lead to define the numeric TLS handshake latency regression threshold that the PQC base image switch must not exceed, then measure TLS handshake latency of PQC-enabled images against it before ship. This resolves a ship-gating open item that the strategy requires to be closed before Sprint 2 ends; it does not change what the base image switch work does, so it runs in parallel with the compliance coordination chain.\n31\t\n32\t## Scope\n33\t\n34\t- Define the numeric maximum acceptable TLS handshake time regression for the PQC base image switch, with the PM and Performance team lead as decision owners (reference points: Chrome ~10% maximum TLS handshake time regression; the Red Hat PQC benchmarking outcome in PSASTRAT-7170).\n35\t- Measure TLS handshake latency for representative PQC-enabled images (e.g., `ubi9/ubi-minimal-pqc`-based) versus their non-PQC predecessors, covering the opportunistic hybrid key exchange path (X25519MLKEM768) and the backwards-compatible classic ECDHE path.\n36\t- Record a pass/fail determination against the defined threshold and, if the threshold is exceeded, a recommendation for remediation work (which would be scoped separately).\n37\t- Confirm opportunistic hybrid key exchange keeps non-PQC TLS 1.3 clients working via classic ECDHE (NFR: Backwards compatibility).\n38\t\n39\t## Acceptance Criteria\n40\t\n41\t- A numeric TLS handshake regression threshold is defined and recorded, with PM and Performance team lead sign-off, before Sprint 2 ends.\n42\t- Measured TLS handshake latency regression for PQC-enabled images is recorded against the threshold, with a pass/fail determination, before ship.\n43\t- Backwards compatibility is confirmed: clients that do not support PQC continue to work via classic ECDHE (no functional regression beyond the accepted latency threshold).\n44\t\n45\t## HLR Traceability\n46\t\n47\t- No HLR maps directly to this epic; it resolves the strategy's Performance NFR (\"NEEDS DOMAIN INPUT\") and the \"Performance Team Support: Required\" prerequisite (TLS handshake latency regression measurement needed before ship).\n48\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac1ecaaf3df4b37e","agent_id":"a3b5f159801f9c1af","session_id":"12e54bbc-7543-4961-a6e8-72b51d0a133c","uuid":"2ce205f7-08e6-4172-a9ff-07ea8abfd491","timestamp":"2026-10-22T11:53:21.469Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b2196225c1eb4daa","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8001 decomposition"}
