{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8370fda2d11b4736","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8001-BRANCH-B-E006\n3\ttitle: Coordinate OCP exception filings for images without available PQC base images\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8001\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Platform Security\n6\tteam: RHOAI PM\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: B\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8001-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8001-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: remove\n15\t  fallback_approach: If all PQC base image variants and the RHEL 9.8 rebase are confirmed\n16\t    available in time, affected teams switch base images instead and no exception\n17\t    coordination is needed for those groups (TLS-stack-blocked components still file\n18\t    exceptions)\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 1\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n23\t  existing_foundation: 1\n24\t  open_questions: 0\n25\t  external_dependency: 0\n26\t  human_process_gates: -1\n27\t  repo_access: 0\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: Medium\n32\tai_implementability_score: 2\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Coordinate OCP exception filings for images without available PQC base images\n36\t\n37\t*Conditional branch B — applies if PQC variants of the python-311/312/nodejs bases and/or the RHEL 9.8 rebase are not confirmed available before September 15, 2026.*\n38\t\n39\t## Description\n40\t\n41\tWhen the PQC base image availability investigation determines that one or more unconfirmed dependencies will not be available in time, this epic drives the OCP exception path for the affected image groups: identifying the affected component teams, directing them to the OCPEXCEPT template, and ensuring each files an exception by September 15, 2026 documenting why the image cannot comply and providing a remediation plan (component TLS stack and reason it cannot negotiate ML-KEM). This branch also covers teams already expected to file exceptions for TLS-stack reasons — fms-guardrails-orchestrator (rustls+ring), TrustyAI explainability service (Java/NSS, JDK 29 timeline September 2027), and the dashboard nodejs image if no PQC variant eventuates — as well as any RHEL9-ELS-based teams blocked by a slipped rebase.\n42\t\n43\t## Scope\n44\t\n45\t- Identify all component teams whose images lack an available PQC base image by the deadline (python/nodejs-based images without variants; RHEL9-ELS-based images if the AIPCC RHEL 9.8 rebase slips; TLS-stack-blocked components).\n46\t- Direct each affected team to the OCPEXCEPT template and the filing requirement: reason for non-compliance, component TLS stack, and a documented remediation plan (e.g., the fms-guardrails-orchestrator TLS migration spike RHOAIENG-7452; TrustyAI JDK LTS timeline).\n47\t- Track exception filings to acknowledgment, and update the readiness matrix records for images on the exception path.\n48\t- In partial outcomes, only unconfirmed groups follow this path — confirmed groups switch base images instead.\n49\t\n50\t## Acceptance Criteria\n51\t\n52\t- Every affected component team has filed an OCP exception via OCPEXCEPT by September 15, 2026, including the component's TLS stack, the reason it cannot negotiate ML-KEM, and a documented remediation plan.\n53\t- Exception filings are tracked to acknowledgment.\n54\t- Readiness matrix records for exception-path images are updated to reflect the filed exceptions.\n55\t\n56\t## HLR Traceability\n57\t\n58\t- **HLR-2 [P0]**: delivers the exception path for teams unable to comply by September 15.\n59\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ac1ecaaf3df4b37e","agent_id":"a3b5f159801f9c1af","session_id":"12e54bbc-7543-4961-a6e8-72b51d0a133c","uuid":"d4e79fa0-5760-48f8-b5e6-c3783115c5ce","timestamp":"2026-10-22T11:53:27.277Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8370fda2d11b4736","permiss