{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9ab7d7b39a245608","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8001-E004\n3\ttitle: Track component team compliance and enforce the September 15 deadline\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8001\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Platform Security\n6\tteam: RHOAI PM\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8001-E003\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8001-E001\n12\tgate_failure_impact:\n13\t  action: rewrite\n14\t  fallback_approach: If PQC variants or the RHEL 9.8 rebase are not confirmed available\n15\t    in time, close-out verification shifts from rebuilt images to filed OCP exceptions\n16\t    for those image groups\n17\tai_signals:\n18\t  change_specificity: 1\n19\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n20\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n21\t  existing_foundation: 1\n22\t  open_questions: 0\n23\t  external_dependency: -1\n24\t  human_process_gates: -1\n25\t  repo_access: 0\n26\t  architecture_claims: 1\n27\timplementation_type: null\n28\tinvestigation_signals: null\n29\tai_implementability: Medium\n30\tai_implementability_score: 1\n31\tjira_key: null\n32\tbranch: null\n33\t---\n34\t# Track component team compliance and enforce the September 15 deadline\n35\t\n36\t## Description\n37\t\n38\tRun the strategy's core coordination mandate: aggregate every component team's compliance status via tracking tickets linked to RHAISTRAT-8001, drive teams to completion, and enforce the September 15, 2026 deadline so that zero RHOAI component images are left unaccounted for — every image has either been rebuilt on a PQC-enabled base image or has a filed, acknowledged OCP exception with a remediation plan. This epic delivers the aggregated compliance view for OCP 5.0 visibility and the close-out audit.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Ensure every component team has a tracking ticket linked to RHAISTRAT-8001, providing the aggregated compliance view (per-image accounting comes from the PQC Readiness Matrix).\n43\t- Send weekly reminders to teams with outstanding switch or exception work; escalate to leadership (per the Mara/Devin sync decision) for teams at risk of missing the deadline without a filed exception.\n44\t- Verify that OCP exception filings include the component's TLS stack, the reason it cannot negotiate ML-KEM, and a documented remediation plan.\n45\t- Close out by September 15, 2026: audit that zero unaccounted-for images remain — each image is either rebuilt on a PQC-enabled base or covered by a filed, acknowledged exception.\n46\t- Verification of switched images: inside any switched container, `update-crypto-policies --show` reports `DEFAULT:PQ` and `openssl list -kem-algorithms` shows ML-KEM-512/768/1024, measured by an automated CI scan across the RHOAI 3.6 payload. Note: TLS-scanner CI tooling is owned by the separate Central TLS Profile strategy (RHAISTRAT-7816); this epic consumes, and does not build, that scan infrastructure. On FIPS-mode clusters, FIPS policy deactivates PQC for this release — that is expected behavior, not a compliance failure. This criterion applies to OpenSSL-backed components only.\n47\t\n48\t## Acceptance Criteria\n49\t\n50\t- All component team tracking tickets are linked to RHAISTRAT-8001, providing an aggregated compliance view for OCP 5.0 (AC-3).\n51\t- By September 15, 2026: every RHOAI component image has either (a) been rebuilt on a PQC-enabled base image, or (b) a filed and acknowledged OCP exception in OCPEXCEPT with a documented remediation plan including the component's TLS stack and reason it cannot negotiate ML-KEM — zero unaccounted-for images remain (AC-2).\n52\t- For OpenSSL-backed switched images, the crypto-policy verification (`DEFAULT:PQ`, ML-KEM kem algorithms listed) is confirmed across the RHOAI 3.6 payload (AC-1, consuming CI scan tooling owned by RHAISTRAT-7816).\n53\t- Weekly reminder cadence and leadership escalation for at-risk teams are demonstrably exercised between now and the deadline.\n54\t\n55\t## HLR Traceability\n56\t\n57\t- **HLR-1 [P0]**: verifies and enforces that all RHOAI runtime images use a PQC-enabled base image (or are covered per below).\n58\t- **HLR-2 [P0]**: enforces the exception path — teams unable to comply by September 15 file an OCP exception with a remediation plan.\n59\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9b2646fd9a047d87","agent_id":"a379f05c2d4fd22a0","session_id":"12e54bbc-7543-4961-a6e8-72b51d0a133c","uuid":"f89dc4d8-0649-46e3-a1f8-e15aeb175a3c","timestamp":"2026-10-22T11:58:37.651Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9ab7d7b39a245608","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8001 decomposition"}
