ation because the strategy explicitly flags it \"NEEDS DOMAIN INPUT\" with owners (PM + Performance team lead) and a resolution deadline (before Sprint 2 ends); runs in parallel. |","new_string":"| E001 → E003 | Rule 3 (Investigation gates downstream) | The readiness matrix's per-image remediation path (switch vs. exception) for ~45 python/nodejs-based and RHEL9-ELS-based images is determined by the investigation outcome. True gate: `rewrite` — matrix content changes, epic exists either way. |\n| E003 → E004 | Rule 12/13 (artifact consumer) | Deadline enforcement and the \"zero unaccounted images\" close-out audit consume the readiness matrix as the per-image accounting artifact. |\n| E001 → E004 | Rule 3 (gated work, direct edge) | E004's `gated_by` target: its close-out verification content (rebuilt images vs. filed OCP exceptions) is determined by the investigation outcome. Kept as a direct edge (not only transitively via E003) so automated consumers detect the gate from the `dependencies` list. |\n| E001 → BRANCH-A-E006 | Rule 3 (conditional branch) | Branch A only exists if PQC variants and the rebase are confirmed in time (bounded outcome, ≤3 possibilities → conditional branch). |\n| E002 → BRANCH-A-E006 | Rule 13 / epic boundary (same surface) | Branch A builds on the build-pipeline base-image wiring for the same build configuration surface; serial to avoid two epics editing the same pipeline configuration independently. |\n| E003 → BRANCH-A-E006 | Rule 12/13 (artifact producer → consumer) | Branch A updates readiness matrix records for the switched image groups — the matrix must exist before those updates can be made. |\n| E001 → BRANCH-B-E006 | Rule 3 (conditional branch) | Branch B only exists if variants/rebase are not available in time; affected teams are directed to the OCP exception path. |\n| E003 → BRANCH-B-E006 | Rule 12/13 (artifact producer → consumer) | Branch B updates readiness matrix records for exception-path images — the matrix must exist be