{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b35fe72cfd0111ba","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8001-BRANCH-A-E006\n3\ttitle: Integrate confirmed PQC variant base images into the build pipeline and coordinate\n4\t  team switches\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8001\n6\tcomponent: Build and Release\n7\tteam: DevOps/Build\n8\ttype: Implementation\n9\tpriority: P0\n10\tbranch: A\n11\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8001-E001\n12\tdependencies:\n13\t- RHAISTRAT-8001-E001\n14\t- RHAISTRAT-8001-E002\n15\t- RHAISTRAT-8001-E003\n16\tgate_failure_impact:\n17\t  action: remove\n18\t  fallback_approach: If PQC variants and the RHEL 9.8 rebase are not confirmed available\n19\t    before the deadline, this switch-path work does not happen; affected image groups\n20\t    follow the OCP exception path instead (partial outcomes switch only confirmed\n21\t    groups)\n22\tai_signals:\n23\t  change_specificity: 1\n24\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n25\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n26\t  existing_foundation: 1\n27\t  open_questions: 0\n28\t  external_dependency: -1\n29\t  human_process_gates: 0\n30\t  repo_access: 1\n31\t  architecture_claims: 1\n32\timplementation_type: null\n33\tinvestigation_signals: null\n34\tai_implementability: High\n35\tai_implementability_score: 4\n36\tjira_key: null\n37\t---\n38\t# Integrate confirmed PQC variant base images into the build pipeline and coordinate team switches\n39\t\n40\t*Conditional branch A — applies if PQC variants of the python-311/312/nodejs bases and/or the RHEL 9.8 rebase are confirmed available before September 15, 2026.*\n41\t\n42\t## Description\n43\t\n44\tWhen the PQC base image availability investigation confirms that PQC variants of `ubi9/python-311`, `ubi9/python-312`, `ubi9/nodejs-22` and/or the RHEL 9.8 rebase (enabling `rhel9-8-els/pqc-minimal` adoption) will be available in time, this epic wires those newly confirmed base images into the RHOAI build pipeline — extending the pipeline enablement already in place for the confirmed bases — and coordinates the affected component teams' final-runtime-stage switches. Affected images: ~10 python-based training variants/lmes-job/feature-server images, 1 nodejs-based dashboard image, and ~34 RHEL9-ELS-based notebooks/workbenches/training-runtime/mlserver images.\n45\t\n46\t## Scope\n47\t\n48\t- Integrate each newly confirmed PQC base image variant into the RHOAI build pipeline, building on the base image pipeline updates already established for the confirmed PQC bases.\n49\t- Notify the owning component teams of each confirmed variant (python-311: 5 training/lmes-job images; python-312: 4 training variants; python-312-minimal: feature-server; nodejs-22: dashboard; RHEL9-ELS group post-rebase) to switch their final runtime stage.\n50\t- Update the readiness matrix records for the switched image groups.\n51\t- For any group in a partial outcome (some variants confirmed, others not), coordinate the switch only for confirmed groups — unconfirmed groups follow the OCP exception path instead.\n52\t\n53\t## Acceptance Criteria\n54\t\n55\t- Each confirmed PQC base image variant is referenceable by RHOAI component builds in the build pipeline.\n56\t- Affected component teams are notified with the specific target base image for their images and the final-stage-only constraint (only the runtime stage changes; no builder image change — HLR-3).\n57\t- Readiness matrix records for the switched groups are updated to reflect the confirmed path.\n58\t- Switched images report `DEFAULT:PQ` via `update-crypto-policies --show` and list ML-KEM-512/768/1024 via `openssl list -kem-algorithms` (OpenSSL-backed components).\n59\t\n60\t## HLR Traceability\n61\t\n62\t- **HLR-1 [P0]**: delivers the switch path for the python/nodejs-based and RHEL9-ELS-based image groups when their PQC bases are confirmed.\n63\t- **HLR-3 [P0]**: switches are final-runtime-stage-only.\n64\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-82463234dec7213e","agent_id":"a762836ed961a9ea0","session_id":"12e54bbc-7543-4961-a6e8-72b51d0a133c","uuid":"781f5cf9-be6e-445b-b535-d606a2fc24b8","timestamp":"2026-10-22T12:04:17.966Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b35fe72cfd0111ba","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8001 decomposition"}
