{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a261f640eb7963fd","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# RHAISTRAT-8001-E005 — Implementation Signal Rationale\n2\t\n3\t| Signal | Value | Rationale |\n4\t|--------|-------|-----------|\n5\t| change_specificity | +1 | The deliverables are concrete and specific: a recorded numeric TLS handshake regression threshold, latency measurements for named PQC-enabled images (e.g., `ubi9/ubi-minimal-pqc`-based) versus their non-PQC predecessors on the X25519MLKEM768 hybrid and classic ECDHE paths, and a recorded pass/fail determination. |\n6\t| pattern_precedent | 0 | No existing latency-benchmark harness or measurement pattern in the platform's repos to copy; the benchmark approach must be assembled for this epic. |\n7\t| adapter_pattern | 0 | Standalone measurement and reporting work — there is no existing plug-in point or adapter surface to extend. |\n8\t| existing_foundation | 0 | The PQC base images to measure are available (confirmed `ubi9/ubi-minimal-pqc`), but no existing measurement tooling, harness, or report format exists in-repo to build on. |\n9\t| open_questions | -1 | The numeric regression threshold is undefined — the strategy marks it \"NEEDS DOMAIN INPUT\" with the PM and Performance team lead as owners; the pass/fail criterion cannot be finalized until that decision lands. |\n10\t| external_dependency | 0 | No external team blocks the work; reference data is readable (PSASTRAT-7170 Red Hat PQC benchmarking outcome, the Chrome ~10% handshake regression reference, the IETF hybrid key exchange draft). |\n11\t| human_process_gates | -1 | The threshold requires PM + Performance team lead sign-off before Sprint 2 ends — a human decision gate on the deliverable, though the measurement itself proceeds without it. |\n12\t| repo_access | 0 | Benchmarks run against pulled container images and produce a report; no platform repo changes are required. |\n13\t| architecture_claims | 0 | The epic